# Architecture Drift Check

Run the drift check when changes touch backend/frontend architecture boundaries, Agent/RAG orchestration, permission/security, DB schema, dependencies, deployment topology, API contracts, or model-provider behavior.

1. Read `docs/architecture/ARCHITECTURE_BASELINE.md`.
2. Run checklist in `docs/architecture/ARCHITECTURE_DRIFT_CHECK.md`.
3. If drift is detected, document in PLAN/TASK or create an ADR under `docs/decisions/`.

For XS/S docs-only, copy, style, test-only, or local validation changes with no architecture impact, note that drift check was not required.

Key invariants:

- Controller → Service → Mapper layering
- Agent Tool → Service (never Mapper directly)
- Backend owns all AI API calls
- RAG answers include sources
- Agent execution writes trace
